Subject: [PATCH] a mage only conjures food and water it can use

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

The mage strategy added by 0015 asks for conjure food and water, but the
highest known spell rank can produce a product above the mage's level. The
normal CanUseItem check intentionally permits conjured products in that path,
so the no-food/no-drink trigger never sees a usable stack and the mage casts
again forever. Bound the rank choice by the product's RequiredLevel as well as
the normal item usability check. Lower ranks remain available, so a level 47
mage with rank 7 also knows how to make the level 45 product it can consume.

WHAT THIS PATCH DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO

It does not change the trigger, the action names, or the party's surplus
conjure rows. It only prevents the spell-name resolver from selecting a
product the caster cannot use.

WHEN THIS PATCH SHOULD BE DELETED

The moment upstream rejects a conjure product whose RequiredLevel is above the
caster's level in this selection path, this hunk is redundant and should be
removed with the corresponding source-contract test.

diff --git a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/GenericSpellActions.cpp b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/GenericSpellActions.cpp
index 57c69ed6..ca9df56a 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/GenericSpellActions.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/GenericSpellActions.cpp
@@ -167,7 +167,14 @@ bool CastSpellAction::Execute(Event /*event*/)
 
             uint32 itemId = spellInfo->Effects[0].ItemType;
             ItemTemplate const* proto = sObjectMgr->GetItemTemplate(itemId);
-            if (!proto || bot->CanUseItem(proto) != EQUIP_ERR_OK)
+            // CanUseItem deliberately treats conjured food and drink as usable
+            // before the character has reached the product's RequiredLevel.
+            // That makes a mage with a higher-rank spell create items it cannot
+            // consume, so the no-food/no-drink trigger never clears. Keep the
+            // rank selection bounded by both the normal item check and the
+            // product's explicit level requirement.
+            if (!proto || proto->RequiredLevel > bot->GetLevel() ||
+                bot->CanUseItem(proto) != EQUIP_ERR_OK)
                 continue;
 
             if (spellInfo->Id > castId)
